Maintainer: Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>
# debhelper only. The package installs a pre-built, self-contained JavaScript
# bundle (packaging/cli-bundle/index.js, produced by `npm run bundle:cli`), so
# nothing is compiled here. That is deliberate: Launchpad's build farm has no
# outbound network access, and a Node build would need the npm registry for the
# TypeScript/ncc toolchain. Bundling on the maintainer's machine keeps the
# builder offline-clean and keeps ~66 MB of build-time node_modules out of the
# source package.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Dhiva-Labs/dl-sentinel
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dlsentinel
Architecture: all
# The bundle is plain JavaScript with no native code, hence Architecture: all.
#
# nodejs (>= 18) rather than (>= 20): the upstream project declares Node 20 in
# package.json, but that floor is the development toolchain's, not the shipped
# CLI's. The bundled CLI was verified against noble's own nodejs 18.19.1 —
# version, rule listing and a full scan all behave identically — and noble ships
# no nodejs newer than 18, so a >= 20 dependency would make this package
# uninstallable on a stock Ubuntu 24.04 system.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs (>= 18)
Description: Security scanner for secrets, dependencies, code and infrastructure
 DL Sentinel scans a repository for exposed secrets, vulnerable dependencies,
 insecure source-code patterns, container and infrastructure misconfiguration,
 API definition security issues and smart-contract risk patterns, then reports
 structured findings as terminal output, JSON, Markdown or SARIF 2.1.0.
 .
 Scanning runs entirely on the local machine. Source code is never uploaded,
 scanned code is never executed, and secret values are redacted before they can
 reach a finding, a report or a log line. The scanner makes no network request
 at all unless a network-backed vulnerability data source is explicitly enabled
 in configuration.
 .
 The catalogue ships 88 rules across six scanners, most of them mapped to CWE
 and OWASP Top 10 (2021) identifiers. Baselines let the tool be adopted on an
 existing codebase and fail only on newly introduced findings, which together
 with CI-friendly exit codes makes it usable as a pipeline gate.
 .
 This package provides the command-line scanner. The self-hosted API server and
 web dashboard are not included.
